# The own-key filter under `A` refuses its walk and the `Cfg[*]` loop places the refusal's marker into `x`
# beside the keys. `%x != Resources.*.Properties.Missing` compares the marker against a right-hand side the
# document lacks under a resource whose key is three hundred right-to-left overrides: the record leads with
# the absence, whose reason names the key and the path. Both are escaped first and cut on the printed width,
# so the console's `Error =` line stays under its whole-line bound and the refusal is printed on it.
rule bidi_key { Cfg[ x | Kind == 'k' ] !empty  Cfg[*][ x | Mode exists or Kind == 'k' ].Sub[*][ s | R1_the_own_key_of_the_sub_map_whose_name_is_long_enough_to_carry_the_refusal_past_the_bound !exists ] !empty or Cfg.Fallback exists  %x != Resources.*.Properties.Missing }
